<title>GREECE: Greek 1M ATHIBOR eases to 11.99 from 12.01 pct.</title>
<headline>Greek 1M ATHIBOR eases to 11.99 from 12.01 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens Interbank Offered Rate (Athibor) for one month dropped to 11.99 from 12.01 percent and the bid rate (Athibid) declined to 11.50 from 11.52 percent.</p>
<p>ATHIBOR</p>
<p> DATE     1-MTH   2-MTH   3-MTH   6-MTH   9-MTH   12-MTH</p>
<p> Feb  26  11.99   11.92   11.83   11.62   11.51   11.43</p>
<p> Feb  25  12.01   11.94   11.83   11.61   11.50   11.43</p>
<p> Feb  20  12.03   11.99   11.88   11.68   11.60   11.49</p>
<p> Feb  19  12.05   11.99   11.88   11.69   11.60   11.50</p>
<p> Feb  18  12.03   11.97   11.84   11.62   11.51   11.44</p>
<p> Feb  17  12.01   11.96   11.85   11.62   11.52   11.45</p>
<p> Feb  13  12.13   12.01   11.04   11.64   11.53   11.46</p>
<p> Feb  12  12.09   11.98   11.83   11.63   11.56   11.46</p>
<p>ATHIBID</p>
<p> Feb  26  11.50   11.43   11.34   11.13   11.04   10.96</p>
<p> Feb  25  11.52   11.45   11.35   11.13   11.03   10.95</p>
<p> Feb  20  11.56   11.50   11.40   11.20   11.13   11.01</p>
<p> Feb  19  11.59   11.50   11.40   11.21   11.13   11.02</p>
<p> Feb  18  11.56   11.49   11.35   11.13   11.03   10.96</p>
<p> Feb  17  11.53   11.47   11.35   11.13   11.03   10.96</p>
<p> Feb  13  11.64   11.52   11.35   11.15   11.04   10.98</p>
<p> Feb  07  11.61   11.50   11.38   11.17   11.07   11.00</p>
<p>Note: ATHIBOR is Greece's official reference rate. It comprises 18 leading state and private banks committed to quoting their rates by 0900 GMT every day.</p>
<p>--Margarita Sotiropoulou, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
